        "text": "Gaussian tail bounds. For a Gaussian variable with mean μ and variance σ², P(|X − μ| ≥ βσ) ≤ exp(−β²/2) for any β > 0 (Theorem 2.12, after Srinivas et al.). For a Gaussian with nonpositive mean, E(X·I(X ≥ 0)) = σ/√(2π) · exp(−μ²/(2σ²)) (Theorem 2.13), the expectation of X restricted to its nonnegative values.",
