        "text": "Posterior inference. With data D of n points, a zero-mean GP prior and Gaussian observation noise of variance σ_n², the posterior mean is μ(x | D) = k(x, X)(k(X, X) + σ_n² I)⁻¹ Y and the posterior covariance is k(x, x) − k(x, X)(k(X, X) + σ_n² I)⁻¹ k(X, x) (Eqs. 4.2 and 4.3); a footnote notes that in practice the prior mean is often set to zero.",
